# Let the taOS controller set the panel brightness.
#
# WHY: the brightness slider in the lock screen's pull-down shade is served by
# the controller, which runs as `taos` (uid 999). The kernel ships
# /sys/class/backlight/*/brightness as root:root 0644 -- readable by anyone,
# writable by root alone -- so without this the slider can show the current
# level and change nothing. Measured on the handset before writing this:
#   -rw-r--r-- root root /sys/class/backlight/ae94000.dsi.0/brightness
#   brightness 2866, max_brightness 4095
#
# WHY THE `video` GROUP AND NOT `uaccess`: TAG+="uaccess" hands access to the
# user of the ACTIVE SEAT via logind ACLs, and this controller's session is
# `manager-early` rather than an active seat session -- the same reason logind
# answers "challenge" to its power-off requests. Group ownership does not depend
# on seat state, and `taos` is already in `video` (23=input, 27=video), so this
# grants nothing that user did not already have for the rest of the display
# stack. It is also exactly what brightnessctl's own packaging does.
#
# SCOPE: the brightness attribute only. max_brightness stays read-only, because
# nothing should ever be writing it.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="backlight", \
    RUN+="/bin/chgrp video /sys/class/backlight/%k/brightness", \
    RUN+="/bin/chmod g+w /sys/class/backlight/%k/brightness"
